%% Diagram: Snowflake 3-layer architecture
%% Source lecture: Snowflake Complete Masterclass - Section 3 (Architecture)
%% Description:  Three independently-scalable layers: Cloud Services (brain),
%%               Compute (virtual warehouses), and Storage (columnar micro-partitions
%%               on S3 / Azure Blob / GCS).  Each layer can be sized & paid for
%%               independently.
%% Author: Prem Vishnoi <pvishnoi@avilx.com>
```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph CS["☁️ Cloud Services (the brain)"]
        META["Metadata Manager<br/>(tables, schemas, users)"]
        OPT["Query Optimizer"]
        SEC["Security & Access Control<br/>(RBAC, masking, row-access)"]
        TXN["Transaction Manager<br/>(ACID across warehouses)"]
    end

    subgraph CMP["⚙️ Compute (virtual warehouses)"]
        W1["XS warehouse<br/>(section 2 demo)"]
        W2["M warehouse<br/>(ELT workloads)"]
        W3["Multi-cluster warehouse<br/>(concurrency)"]
    end

    subgraph STG["💾 Storage (columnar micro-partitions)"]
        S3["S3 / Azure Blob / GCS<br/>(same buckets used by all warehouses)"]
    end

    USER[SQL client / driver] --> CS
    CS  --> W1
    CS  --> W2
    CS  --> W3
    W1  <--> S3
    W2  <--> S3
    W3  <--> S3

    style CS  fill:#E0F2FE,stroke:#0369A1
    style CMP fill:#FEF3C7,stroke:#B45309
    style STG fill:#DCFCE7,stroke:#166534
```
